Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Description ", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966866805854064*^9, 
  3.9668668148638163`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5f553301-9271-4913-a8cb-\
6531146eb94f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compute \n1. diffuse supernova neutrino background (DSNB) flux for electron \
antineutrinos ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Nu]", "e"], "_"]],
  CellChangeTimes->{3.946674566516795*^9},ExpressionUUID->
  "20d8a301-f8a3-4ff0-a184-9af74a71dc3b"],
 "  for binary synthesis (Horiuchi et al. 2021), progen+engine data (Kresse \
et al. 2021), and no binaries (Horiuchi et al. 2021). \n\tby incorporating \
direct black hole BH contribution (failed supernova) based on Horiuchi et al. \
2021, which previously computed binary contribution with only neutron star \
formation NS contribution to DSNB.\n\tDone by applying 2 parameter criterion \
(\[Mu]4 as function of  \[Mu]4*M4) from Ertl et al. 2016 OR 1 parameter \
criterion (only  \[Mu]4) to 1D CCSN simulation outcomes from Kresse et al. \
2021 (knows BH vs NS) to \t\t\tdistinguish BH vs NS. \n\tUsing this \
criterion, it can be applied to the binary synthesis and no binary synthesis \
(Horiuchi et al. 2021) which is blind to BH vs NS\n\t*Note that all \
calculations is without outliers (i.e. bin syn \[Mu]4 or \[Mu]4*M4 data \
outside range of progen+engine data are outliers)\n\t**Note that Lunardini et \
al. 2025 did this but in a different approach\n2.  energy integrated DSNB \
flux\n3. event rates at Super-kamiokande Gadollinium doped SK-Gd, \
Hyper-Kamiokande, and JUNO\n4. final tables and plots for fiducial model \
(with spread, i.e. models with max or min integrated DSNB)"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966883096016415*^9, 3.966883148850246*^9}, {
   3.966883184757092*^9, 3.966883505316596*^9}, 3.966883564113179*^9, {
   3.9668842855372677`*^9, 3.966884496148212*^9}, {3.9668846123879433`*^9, 
   3.966884745714493*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"fcc5ba0b-50ee-4dcc-957e-\
79b5660087d0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["unlike version 14 a complete loop of this computation is performed \
for any combo of \n",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "1. varying binary synthesis models\n2. varying engine models\n3. varying \
maximal NS mass (i.e. baryonic mass of neutron star for BH formation) only \
for fiducial engine model\n4. varying criterion (2 parameter criterion \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]\[Mu]4 as function of  \[Mu]4*M4\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] or 1 parameter criterion \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]\[Mu]4\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]) \n5. with/without \
criterion (i.e. all NS or BH+NS with criterion), already implemented \
internally \n6. without flavor conversions or with flavor conversions (only \
MSW for inverted hierarchy IH or normal hierarchy NH), already implemented \
internally "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96688474780575*^9, 
  3.966884890760538*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f9a97ad3-fdb7-41ea-80ca-\
566fc34db1e3"]
}, Closed]],

