Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Description", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.949228031870182*^9, 
  3.949228036148719*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e0a0ae4c-4864-488c-8ec0-\
00e442d142fa"],

Cell["\<\
Take binary synthesis, apply 2 parameter criterion (linear function \
\[Mu]4[Mco]) to get BH and NS pops, and then get nearest neutrino variables \
from combo (progen_engine) data via 2 parameters (\[Mu]4 and Mco) and tag \
outliers.
by doing the following 
1. bin and split combo (progen+engine) data into NS and BH data and create \
visuals 
2. from the progen+engine data determine the optimal 2 parameter criterion to \
use (that minimizes the number of outliers, via linear regression)
2. bin binary synthesis data and create visuals 
3. Take the binary synthesis data and split into NS and BH based on 2 \
parameter criterion (linear function \[Mu]4[Mco]) 
4. Get the nearest neutrino spectral parameter values in combo data for bin \
syn data 
5. Also check whether each data is an outlier\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.949228038989751*^9, 3.9492280535997972`*^9}, {
  3.9492281191860247`*^9, 3.949228164233204*^9}, {3.949228210262001*^9, 
  3.9492282523193617`*^9}, {3.949228388906193*^9, 3.94922842577459*^9}, {
  3.949228487761814*^9, 
  3.949228516824622*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"44941426-a441-44b6-ae5a-\
799096049bb8"]
}, Closed]],

